<% content_for :title, 'Master credentials & sync' %>
<% content_for :head do %><meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache"><% end %>
<div class="space-y-6">
  <section class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4">
    <div><h1 class="page-title">Master credentials &amp; sync</h1><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-mocha">Set up connections, find what stopped working, and choose the next repair step.</p></div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <%= link_to 'Credential setup', '#credentials', class: 'btn-primary btn-sm' %>
      <%= link_to 'Improvement plan', '#improvements', class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm' %>
      <% if Current.user.can?('sync.read') %><%= link_to 'Sync history', syncs_path, class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm' %><% end %>
      <% if Current.user.can?('system.read') %><%= link_to 'Worker status', system_path, class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm' %><% end %>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card card-pad text-sm text-mocha">
    <p><strong class="text-ink">Save credentials → check access → read once → review freshness.</strong> Choose automatic schedules on each provider's setup page after a successful read.</p>
    <p class="mt-2">Saved credentials and a successful check do not prove that new data is arriving. Credential completeness and source freshness are shown separately.</p>
    <p class="mt-2">Saved secrets stay hidden. Only people with settings-write permission can replace them; platform backup credentials remain with the platform operator. Opening this page starts no checks or syncs.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-label="Sync health" class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl">Sync health &amp; repair</h2>
    <% if @status_notice %><p role="alert" class="flash flash-alert"><%= @status_notice %></p><% end %>
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
      <% @sync_sources.each do |source| %>
        <% active = SourceSyncStatus::ACTIVE_BADGES.include?(source[:badge]) %>
        <article class="card card-pad <%= active ? 'source-sync-active' : 'source-sync-inactive' %> space-y-3" data-connection-source="<%= source[:key] %>">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><h3 class="font-display text-lg"><%= source[:label] %></h3><span class="<%= active ? 'pill-fern' : 'pill-rose' %>"><%= source[:badge] %></span></div>
          <p class="text-sm text-mocha"><%= source[:next_step] %></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-taupe"><%= source[:schedule] %></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-mocha">Last source evidence: <% if source[:last_at] %><time datetime="<%= source[:last_at].iso8601 %>"><%= l(source[:last_at].in_time_zone, format: :short) %></time><% else %>None recorded<% end %></p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <%= link_to 'Review setup', connection_source_setup_path(source), class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm' %>
            <% if connection_source_can_sync?(source) %>
              <% action = source[:key] == 'shopify' ? source_syncs_path(source: 'shopify') : source_sync_path(source[:key]) %>
              <%= button_to source[:mode] == 'portal' ? 'Import portal export' : 'Read source now', action, method: :post, class: 'btn-primary btn-sm', form: { data: { turbo: false } } %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </article>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="credentials" class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl">Credential setup</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-mocha">Each connection keeps its existing credential store. “Configured” means required fields are present, not that vendor access has been checked. Blank secret fields keep their saved values.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <% @services.each do |service| %>
        <section class="card card-pad space-y-3" data-credential-service="<%= service[:key] %>">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2"><h3 class="font-display text-lg"><%= service[:name] %></h3><span class="pill-taupe"><%= service[:state] %></span></div>
          <p class="text-sm text-mocha"><%= service[:description] %></p>
          <% if service[:checked_at] %><p class="text-xs text-taupe">Last access check: <time datetime="<%= service[:checked_at].iso8601 %>"><%= l(service[:checked_at].in_time_zone, format: :short) %></time></p><% end %>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <%= link_to Current.user.can?('settings.write') ? 'Manage setup' : 'View setup', connection_service_setup_path(service), class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm' %>
            <% if service[:checkable] && Current.user.can?('settings.write') %><%= button_to 'Check read access', check_access_pos_connection_path(service[:key]), method: :post, class: 'btn-primary btn-sm', form: { data: { turbo: false } } %><% end %>
            <% if service[:key] == 'square' && service[:state] == 'Configured' && Current.user.can?('sync.write') %><%= button_to 'Read Square now', source_syncs_path(source: 'square'), method: :post, class: 'btn-primary btn-sm', form: { data: { turbo: false } } %><% end %>
          </div>
          <details class="text-sm text-mocha">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-ink">Required access &amp; troubleshooting</summary>
            <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2"><% service[:fields].each do |field| %><li><span class="font-medium"><%= field[:label] %></span>: <%= field[:unreadable] ? 'Unreadable — restore encryption keys' : field[:set] ? 'Saved' : field[:optional] ? 'Optional · not set' : 'Missing · not set' %><% if field[:set] %> · <%= field[:source] %><% end %></li><% end %></ul>
            <p class="mt-3"><%= service[:find_hint] %></p>
            <% if service[:find_url] %><p class="mt-2"><%= link_to 'Open provider setup', service[:find_url], target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer', class: 'underline' %></p><% end %>
            <% if service[:renewal_note] %><p class="mt-3"><strong>Renewal:</strong> <%= service[:renewal_note] %></p><% end %>
          </details>
        </section>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="improvements" class="card card-pad space-y-4">
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl">Sync improvement plan</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-4 text-sm text-mocha">
      <li><strong class="text-ink">1. One setup desk — available in this change.</strong> Named credential forms, saved-field indicators, explicit access checks, source reads and repair guidance. Existing permissions and schedules stay in place.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">2. Explain every failure — next.</strong> Give every connector the same last-attempt, last-success, error category, next retry and job status. Separate vendor access blocks from bad credentials and worker failures. Add stale-source alerts and verified receipt coverage.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">3. Make maintenance predictable — planned.</strong> Record a responsible person, review dates and vault references; coordinate shared-key rotation, verify recovery and add provider-approved automatic feeds. Require a successful read and reconciliation before activating a new schedule.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-sm text-mocha">If a check succeeds but data stays stale, review the last job in Sync history and ask the platform operator to inspect Worker status. A reporting login does not grant payment-write access or make manual portal data automatic.</p>
    <p class="text-xs text-taupe">Platform operators manage hosting, encryption and database credentials separately. Restore existing encryption keys from the protected backup if stored credentials become unreadable.</p>
  </section>
</div>
